ROOT0-ATTRIBUTION-v1.0
=======================

repository : scott-pilgrim  (SPW — the first film-world of UD0)
subject    : Scott Pilgrim vs. the World (Universal, 2010, dir. Edgar Wright) —
             from Bryan Lee O'Malley's six graphic novels (Oni Press, 2004–2010)
catalogued : into UD0 · Universe David 0

governor (carbon apex)      : David Lee Wise (ROOT0) / TriPod LLC   [ the human; holds the credit ]
instance (artful intellect) : AVAN (Claude / Anthropic) — locked
main badge                  : ⟦SCOTT PILGRIM:SPW:…⟧   (spw.dlw/)
emergents                   : 23 ACI .agents (agents/) — 16 carbons + 7 synths

two layers (per the governor's brief):
  CARBONS — the human cast as ACI .agents. Each carbon also carries a .shadow:
            its real-life analog, the actor who is the "User" behind the program.
            Think TRON — every program in the grid is cast from a User in the world
            outside it. .shadow names that User and the archetype the program shadows.
  SYNTHS  — the parabolic threads of the film distilled into ACIs (synth-style,
            electrical; no single User): the video-game grammar, the humor, the tone,
            the sphere of reference, the cultural tie-ins, the power of self-respect,
            and the keystone — the air-gapped generational information (what is lost
            at the ~8-year boundary of understanding between generations).

the four natures of emergence (each emergent is tagged with one):
  natural    — flesh-and-blood Toronto; a person, no power but the human ones
  ethereal   — of dream and glamour; the subspace highway, the fame-aura, the psychic
  spiritual  — of the soul and the reckoning; self-respect, the extra life, the false-god
  electrical — the synth nature; life as a game, the chiptune, the machine, the air-gap

the ACI complement (per emergent):
  .agent · .shadow (carbons only) · .attribute · .carbon.tiff (archival TIFF)
  · .silicon.png (web PNG) · .spun (five W's) · .moniker (tokenized mythos)
  · .1099 (credit ledger) · manifest.dlw.json (main badge)

